  "title": "nvme: fix Coverity Operands don't affect result",
  "description": "Fix Coverity Operands don't affect result warning.\n\nIn this case it was a clear minor coding bug.\n\nThe Coverity warning correctly identifies that `((sc & 0x1fe) >> 9)` will always result in 0 because `sc` is a 16-bit value and `0x1fe` (binary 0000 0001 1111 1110) does not have any bits set at or above the 9th bit position.\n\nIn the NVMe specification, the Status Field of a CQE is located in DW3 (bits 31:16). Within that field:\n- Bits 24:17 represent the Status Code (SC).\n\nThe variable `sc` is fetched using `tvb_get_uint16(nvme_tvb, 14, ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN)`. In a standard 16-byte NVMe CQE, offset 14 corresponds to the start of DW3 bits 31:16.\n\nTo extract the Status Code (SC), which occupies bits 1 through 8 of that 16-bit word, the mask should be `0x1fe` and the shift should be **1**, not 9.\n\nCoverity CID 1485993\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
